\begin_layout Standard
There are numerous complexity taxonomies already in use, including
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
dimensionality mathematical of the room (curse of dimensionality)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
amount of free parameters (neural networks)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
computational runtime complexity (floating point operations per second,
 Bachmann–Landau notation, ...)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
computation tree related (amount of nodes, weighted nodes, branching factor,
 ...)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
human-specific (chunks of knowledge, plausibility in context, personalized
 weighting ...)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The many subdivision possibilities cannot be summarised in a simple and
 contradiction-free paradigm.
 In GP, therefore, no further distinction is usually made between interpretabili
ty and the (weighted) number of nodes.
 
