\begin_layout Standard
We will evaluate our approach offline on transition samples, which will
 be subject to a symbolic regression.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The fitness is calculated in the form of the regression error, which is
 the sum of the distance between the outouts and predicted values of a data
 set.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Both the mean average error (MAE) and the mean square error (MSE) are widely
 used distance measurements for this purpose.
 The MAE is widely used in GP, as it indicates the average deviation from
 the target solution and is distance-true.
 The MSE squares the distance and thus is not distance-true, making it a
 less honest indicator.
 The MSE, however, iseverely punishes outliers, lumps of strong deviation
 and volatile solutions, which can lead to a better overall generalisation.
 
\end_layout

