\begin_layout Section
Fixed Nodes
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "subsec:Fixed-nodes"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Fixed nodes were implemented in addition to the TED, which has shown in
 a very early stage to loose its protective effect for very small trees.
 Therefore, the expert has the chance to manually select nodes that should
 not be affected by the GP process in his origin tree.
 By explicitly securing the core structure binds the GP process even more
 closely to the preferences of the developer.
 Especially when the developer is sure of the correctness of his abstraction,
 pointless optimisation attempts of the GP process can be prevented at certain
 points, which reduces the runtime by reducing the search space and can
 also improve the reliability of the programmes.
 For very large trees, fixed nodes might even be mandatory to prevent a
 senseless search in a humonguous search space.
\end_layout

