\begin_layout Chapter
Comparison & Discussion
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In this section, a large number of familiarity-based GP runs are evaluated
 and compared with regular GP runs, six of these are presented in more detail.
 The Pareto candidates found are primarily examined for familiarity and
 interpretability.
 Their performance is compared both in terms of regression error and real
 fitness, but also examined for implications for security.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
All runs were carried out with both MAE and MSE.
 The runs with MSE had in almost all cases the better results in the real
 benchmarks and also allowed them to be better compared with Hein's results.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
Benchmarks
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Both the Mountain car (MC) as well as the Industrial Benchmark (IB) were
 used to evaluate the approach.
 MC is a widely used, simple toy benchmark, where the concept can be tested
 well.
 The IB is, in contrast, a stochastically independent, high-dimensional
 testbed, which was especially designed by scientists at Siemens for the
 simulation of very complex processes in industry for RL.
\end_layout

