\begin_layout Subsection
Simple If-Acceleration with fixed nodes
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The if-condition, including the distinction between Action 0 and 2, is selected
 as fixed core structure to enforce the relatively small origin tree as
 a structure even for complex candidates.
 Since both Sarsa policies choose action 1, the regression error can no
 longer fall to 0.
 However, since we as experts are sure that action 1 is not relevant, this
 restriction is harmless.
 The kernel structure massively restricts the search space for solution
 candidates by the expert and marks expert knowledge as part of the solution
 that no longer needs to be found in the GP process.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The regression error drops to 0.05 and hardly differs from that of unrestricted
 runs.
 This surprisingly good result can probably be achieved thanks to the specialisa
tion on the core heuristic.
\end_layout

