\begin_layout Subsection
Sarsa-75
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\noindent
The lack of experience in Sarsa-75 manifests itself in a worse, but still
 intrinsically more complex policy.
 Not only is the reversal point far more uneven, but the data from an episode
 that fails shortly before the finish must also be taken into account, forming
 a much larger observation space that has to be considered.
 The regression error drops to just below 0.2 for all runs (MSE), MAE runs
 performed worse in terms of both regression error (approx.
 0.25) and real benchmark evaluation (approx.
 5-10 steps).
 
\end_layout

