\begin_layout Subsection
Mountain car Summmary / Analysis
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Since the space of the candidates is artificially changed in familiar GP,
 it is to be expected that the performance is subject to the classic GP,
 but the familiar candidates should be more comprehensible, more similar
 to each other within a run and less volatile in real performance.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The familiar solutions were superior to the regular GP candidates in all
 respects, including the regression error, which is a big surprise in view
 of the reduced degree of freedom.
 The extraordinary performance can probably be explained by the optimised
 search space, which could be reduced to an efficient and smaller space
 by the expert's specification.
 The real fitness of an agent often correlates only slightly with its regression
 error, which Hein has already described in 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "sec:Online-offline_regression"

\end_inset

.
 Even the problem of the first acceleration, which was actually very difficult
 to solve, could be solved.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Besides the performance difference, the Sarsa-75 version behaves very volatile
 and is therefore very difficult to assess (more data/observation space,
 unclear delimitations, easily overfit solutions due to the many wrong decisions
, ...).
\end_layout

